h  the best public image even more so than  usual now you might think that was the  end of the gambling related news for the  weekend but there was more before the  tournament xqc appeared on pokeman's  podcast one of the topics they talked  about was his gambling sqc has regularly  taken part in sponsor gambling streams  over the past year pulling in well over  a hundred thousand viewers at times to  watch him gamble in online casinos and  slot machines we've seen him win big and  lose big but it was on this podcast that  xqc shared just how much money he'd lost  in april this year  is because it's fun because it's fun  it's fun and i can afford it and if  we're doing it just because it's fun  doesn't mean it's okay  would you have as much fun gambling if  you were doing it off stream than on  stream  yeah i i'm the  i gamble every day i lost two million  really  i lost 1.85  of course 1.85 million dollars is a  pretty staggering and inconceivable  amount for most people it's a shocking  number but if you've been paying  attention to the rise of gambling on  twitch over the past year it's not too  unfamiliar big streamers such as train  wrecks have shared their losses before  and talked openly about their need to  win back and chase losses which only  worsens the problem so-called crypto  casinos like stake and rubet are popular  sites for streamers to gamble  cryptocurrencies in front of their  viewers in august 2021 twitch banned the  promotion of gambling games on the  platform but some people felt like this  wasn't enough sometimes the streamers  gamble with their own money sometimes  they gamble with money given to them by  the gambling website but the issue of  course is the people who are watching  there are strict laws internationally  around gambling especially promotion of  it to minors the very people who could  be watching their favorite streamers  doing it now with all that being said it  is important to differentiate the kinds  of gambling happening on twitch and in  the unregulated crypto world versus the  world of regulated gambling in the  regulated world responsible gaming is  taken very seriously and governing  bodies take deliberate steps to help  better with gambling problems however on  twitch not all streamers use these  regulated operators or heed their  messages about playing responsibly it's  also important to note here that xqc  said he was addicted and just like any  addiction it can spiral out of control  without adequate help in july last year  he announced he was quitting online  gambling after becoming addicted to it  and more recently he confirmed he was  still addicted and considered himself to  be ill in a recent phone call on his  stream xqc was scolded by his dad for  the money that he'd lost while gambling  i'm on stream i guess i'm sure i'm sure  now what's up  no no what do you mean what's up except  stop stop now yeah i lost some money  yesterday what about it  you're my little boy  dad stop reading stop reading and  clickbait articles man i lose money  sometimes it happens what about what's  up  solo i mean dad come on now like you  know if  they think  yeah of course i'm fine  the rs  it's important to note here that while  xqc is still gambling just like many  people with addictions he doesn't  condone it and says that other people  shouldn't do the same he said that in  his case it's an illness he can afford  to have because of his privileged  financial position there are and will  continue to be calls for tighter  restrictions around gambling on twitch  it's been one of the most contentious  issues on twitch and continues to fuel  the debate around responsibility whether  it's the streamers twitch or the  gambling sites themselves  you
 

